        "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
        "active_lock_reason": null,
        "body": "### Check for existing issues\r\n\r\n- [X] Completed\r\n\r\n### Describe the feature\r\n\r\nThis is an idea i've had for a while that I've not seen in any code editor *yet*.\r\n\r\nOn macOS we have dynamic wallpapers that can change appearance and color depending on the time of the day, darkest wallpaper being applied at midnight and then a semi-dark/light in the morning,  light during the day and a semi-dark/light at the evening - we could map this to themes - so a theme could \"bundle\" 4 (or more) versions of itself where the user can switch between any of them if they'd like to (as regular) or enable a dynamic option which cycles between them depending on the time of the day.\r\n\r\nAs a bonus; it'd be really nice for themes to have access to the system accent color - which would allow themes to pick the preferred system color for accents in their theme, which i think would also help improve the \"dynamicity\" of themes, at least on macos.\r\n\r\n### Environment\r\n\r\nnone\r\n\r\n### If applicable, add mockups / screenshots to help present your vision of the feature\r\n\r\n\r\n_No response_",
