        "author_association": "NONE",
        "body": "@quartzjer I haven't found workarounds. I'm sure you'll agree that this is not really xclip's fault here. I'm not sure why Xwayland clears the selection during init. I also don't know if this is a wsl specific issue or Weston in general.\r\n\r\nI don't have a Linux setup, so could you check if this also happens in a non-WSL Wayland environment? To see the bug you need to make sure the xclip selection triggers xwayland init (i.e. xwayland must not be init'd until then).  ",
